==========================================================================
O1: can a never-funded address sign a Hedera transaction?
==========================================================================

operator/relay 0.0.10298158  0xd30de9c5aef8079b4718b4988e8fd1d1a96f3115
balance        96870156309 tinybar

virgin signer  0xAE3aF24e344d0296aA5B72510393De828d7eB930   (generated now, never funded)

[C2] control: is the virgin address really unknown to the network?
     mirror node: 404, unknown. PASS, the key is virgin

[A] virgin key with NO Hedera account, gasPrice = 0, relay allowance 2 HBAR
    HIP-410 line 405 predicts this fails: the sender must resolve to an account.
    receipt: INVALID_ACCOUNT_ID
    result            INVALID_ACCOUNT_ID
    charged_tx_fee    133017 tinybar
    relay  0.0.10298158 debited 133017
    signer (no account) debited null
    => signer bore cost or relay paid nothing

[*] creating a hollow account for the virgin address (1 tinybar transfer)
    virgin address is now 0.0.10319674, balance 1 tinybar

[B] same virgin key, now with an account, gasPrice = 0, relay allowance 2 HBAR
    HIP-410 predicts the relay must cover 100 percent.
    result            SUCCESS
    charged_tx_fee    2373000 tinybar
    relay  0.0.10298158 debited 2373000
    signer 0.0.10319674 debited 0
    => SPONSORED, signer paid nothing
    msg.sender recorded as 0x00000000000000000000000000000000009d773a
    alias 0xae3af24e344d0296aa5b72510393de828d7eb930
    long-zero form of 0.0.10319674 is 0x00000000000000000000000000000000009d773a
    MATCHES the virgin key. The sponsored call really came from it.
    NOTE: the public record carries the account NUMBER, not the alias.
    Hedera account numbers are monotonic, so the number dates the account.

[C1] control: operator signs and pays for itself, gasPrice > 0.
     Known answer: the signer IS debited. If this also reads 'sponsored',
     the classifier is broken and B means nothing.
     network gas price 113 tinybar, bidding 2x = 2260000000000 weibar
    result            SUCCESS
    charged_tx_fee    2373000 tinybar
    relay  0.0.10298158 debited 2373000
    signer 0.0.10298158 debited 2373000
    => signer bore cost or relay paid nothing
     PASS, control shows the signer paying

==========================================================================
ANSWER: a registration address needs NO funding of its own. The relay
pays 100 percent. The only on-chain link to it is the dust transfer that
created it, which comes from the relay, not from the trader.
